# Allowlist: the image build sees the Rust workspace, the migrations and the sqlx metadata, and nothing else. No .git, no .env, no docs, no target/.
# rust-toolchain.toml is left out on purpose: the builder image is the pinned toolchain, and the file would make
# rustup download rustfmt and clippy, which a release build does not need.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!crates
# The startup schema check embeds Ledgerly-Java's migrations (crates/shared/build.rs), and sqlx's query macros
# read the offline metadata; .cargo/config.toml tells them to.
!vendor/ledgerly-java/src/main/resources/db/migration
!.sqlx
!.cargo
# Served as Swagger UI's spec in the `local` profile (crates/app/src/docs.rs).
!api/openapi.yaml
